xenoblade's combat can be overwhelming  especially if you aren't used to mmo  style battles so i'm gonna do my very  best to break down the basics of combat  from the beginning of a fight to the  very end at its purest form xenoblade  chronicles 3 is all about managing  meters auto attacks and cooldown timers  fill arts meters while well-timed arts  fill the talent meter and a number of  things such as critical hits and  well-timed arts fill the chain attack  gauge but before we get into the  nitty-gritty let's start with something  broad classes there are three different  types of classes in xenoblade chronicles  3 attacker defender and healer those  roles should be pretty self-explanatory  attackers deal high damage defenders  tank enemies and pull aggro and healers  offer support for your party it's  important to keep a good balance of  these three classes at all times classes  are further divided by faction each  class either falls under kevis or agnes  this symbol in the top right corner lets  you know which faction they belong to  for the most part kevis and agnes  classes play the same except for one key  difference kevs class arts are on a  cooldown timer while the cooldown on  agnes class arts are tied to auto  attacks every class has an auto attack  once you're in range of an enemy your  character will attack at a regular  interval different classes have  different auto attack speeds for example  noah's sword fighter class has a  relatively quick auto attack speed  compared to senna's ogre class depending  on the class successful auto attacks  fill your arts meters arts are powerful  abilities that can inflict a large  amount of damage set up combos and heal  and buff party members early on each  class has five unique arts three of  which can be equipped once an art gauge  is full press the corresponding button  to use it however you shouldn't use an  art the second the gauge is full instead  cancel an auto attack into an art to do  this activate an art right as the weapon  makes contact with the enemy if you  timed it right a circle should appear on  the screen canceling auto attacks into  arts and arts into other arts and arts  into talent arts speeds up your attacks  allowing you to do even more damage  [Music]  different arts serve different purposes  and it's important to check an arts  description in the arts menu whenever  you unlock a new class for many  positioning plays a huge role for  example noah's swordfighter class has  two arts that are more effective with  proper positioning sword strike inflicts  break when directed towards the side of  an enemy while edge thrust gets a nice  damage boost from behind if you're ever  unsure as to which angle you're  attacking an enemy from you can  reference the little arrow in the bottom  right corner an arrow pointing up means  you're facing the enemy an arrow  pointing to the side means you're at the  enemy's side and an arrow pointing down  means you are behind the enemy while  positioning is important for every class  attackers typically require the most  precise positioning think about it if  defenders are successfully drawing enemy  aggro then that should give your  attackers and healers free range of the  battlefield arts can also be used to set  up combos across multiple classes and  party members pulling these off requires  precise timing a well-thought-out party  composition and a bit of rng both combo  strings are initiated by a breaker art  noaa's swordfighter class starts the  game with sword strike which as  mentioned earlier inflicts break with  the proper positioning lance can follow  that up with bulrush the heavy guards  topple art from there you have two  options a burst combo or a smash combo  for a burst combo you'd want to follow  up a topple art with a day's art uni's  medic gunner is your best bet here  finally you'll want to hit the dazed  enemy with a burst art successful burst  combos will strip an enemy of its rage  status and they will drop more loot  alternatively once you've toppled an  enemy you can follow it up with a launch  art which sends an enemy into the air in  this short-lived state enemies become  more vulnerable you can finish off the  combo with a smash art which spikes the  enemy back to the ground and delivers a  nice bit of damage  [Music]  [Music]  fortunately you don't have to manually  initiate each art in order to pull off  one of these combos by default your  party will automatically chase these  combos as long as they have the right  arts equipped and they aren't cooling  down you can even hold zr and press left  on the d-pad to specify which combo  you'd like the party to chase i prefer  to play as an attacker because that  means i can usually kick off the combo  by using a breaker art if you'd rather  carry out these combos manually you can  switch between characters mid-battle by  holding zr and using l r early on you  can't actually complete these combos  because you won't have the proper arts  and classes unlocked there are also some  classes that can't contribute to these  combos with their basic arts so keep  this in mind as you tinker with your  team composition for easy reference  breaker topple days bursts launch and  smash arts all have symbols that  indicate their effect to make things a  little easier as you flip through menus  as you land arts and critical hits your  talent art gauge will fill up this is a  powerful art linked to your specific  class like standard arts these can be  cancelled and have a wide range of  effects some can contribute to the  aforementioned combos others can inflict  debuffs on enemies or they can pull  aggro for example this sword fighter's  overclock buster deals extra damage  today's enemies while the ogre's  pressure drop launches a toppled enemy  okay so now we have the basics of  classes auto attacks arts combos and  talent arts these five pillars account  for the moment-to-moment combat gameplay  land auto attacks cancel auto attacks  into arts chain arts together for combos  and utilize talent arts with that out of  the way let's talk master arts and  fusion arts this is where things get a  little more complicated so bear with me  as you level up different classes with  different characters you will unlock  master arts for specific characters for  example if you change noah's class from  the sword fighter to the zephyr you can  unlock zephyr specific arts that noah  can use regardless of his class there  are some restrictions but this means you  could give noah defender arts even if  you think he makes a better attacker  master arts are mapped to the d-pad  however you'll need to level up to  unlock all three master art slots you  can use master arts the same way you  would regular arts or you could combine  them with regular arts to create fusion  arts when you equip master arts be  mindful of where you equip them because  that will determine which art they will  fuse with master arts map to up on the  d-pad will fuse with art map to x right  on the d-pad will fuse with y and down  on the d-pad will fuse with b in order  to use a fusion art first both the  master art and standard art must be  charged then hold zr and press either x  y or b fusion arts are handy because  they deal more damage they combine  status effects buffs and debuffs from  both arts and they can increase your  interlink level we'll get to that later  keep in mind that unlike regular arts  master arts aren't charged at the  beginning of battle meaning you'll have  to wait a bit before you can utilize  them i typically kick off battle using  my standard arts but once i get the ball  rolling i predominantly use fusion arts  you can also set your party members to  prioritize fusion arts by pressing zl  and right on the d-pad at the beginning  of a battle alright let's circle back on  interlinks now new to xenoblade  chronicles 3 is the interlinking  mechanic this allows two compatible  party members to transform into a cool  mech thing while in this state you deal  extra damage and your arts have no  cooldown the catch is that you can only  stay interlinked for a short period of  time before it overheats like standard  arts interlinked arts can be cancelled  into each other in order to fill up a  different talent art gauge normally if  an interlink overheats both party  members will be kicked out of the state  even if they are mid-attack however if  an interlink overheats during a talent  art the interlink will finish the attack  before ejecting both party members i  typically wait until the very last  second to use my talent art in this form  while different inner links serve  different roles all can deal a hefty  amount of damage if used properly there  is an added wrinkle to interlinking  though your interlink level a number  located in the bottom left corner can  improve the effectiveness of your  interlink if you activate a level 3  interlink some arts may have additional  effects for example noaa and mio's  interlink can deal brake damage on all  enemies if the interlink level is at 3.  it's also worth noting that interlink  level resets at the start of a battle or  once an interlink is severed so how do  you level up an interlink fusion arts of  course while fusion arts are more  effective the main reason you should use  fusion arts is to level up your  interlinks this will make your party a  lot more efficient across the board so  with master arts fusion arts and  interlinking out of the way let's move  on to chain attacks  [Music]  chain attacks are nothing new to the  series but they are different this time  around once the chain attack gauge is  full press plus to initiate it this will  pause the battle and let you choose one  of three chain orders or high damage  attacks that have secondary status  effects in order to carry out one of  these chain orders your tp must exceed  100. to do this each conscious party  member will be allowed to attack once  above each party member's portrait is a  number that number represents the base  amount of tp they can contribute to the  tp gauge this number can vary based on a  handful of factors but it will always  start at the number above the portrait  once you exceed 100 tp the chain order  will carry out and you'll start the  process over again the goal is to get  your tp as high as possible while using  as few characters as possible in order  to carry out multiple chain attacks the  longer you can keep a chain attack going  the more damage you'll deal and the more  experience you'll get afterwards classes  also play an important role in chain  attacks if you begin a chain order with  an attacker you'll get a first blood tp  bonus healers will max out your tp at 99  allowing you to carry out additional  attacks completing a chain order with a  defender will reactivate the party  member with the most tp for the next  chain order you also get atp bonus for  utilizing party members that match the  class of the chain order additionally  you can also carry out smash and burst  combos during chain attacks if you have  the right arts equipped how high you get  your tp determines how many characters  are reactivated for the next chain order  100 to 149 will reactivate one party  member 150 to 199 will reactivate two  and 200 and above will reactivate three  the more party members you manage to  reactivate the longer your chain attack  will last and that pretty much covers  chain attacks  just kidding let's talk about auroboros  orders light gameplay spoilers here in  one  two and three okay once you unlock  interlinks with all party members you  can set up oroboros orders by carrying  out chain orders between two party  members that share an interlink form mio  and noah lans and senna and union tion  once both of those paired off characters  complete a chain order an oroboros order  will appear in the chain order selection  screen choosing an oroboros order will  reactivate every party member once  you've maxed out the tp gauge your  interlinked party members will carry out  an incredibly powerful attack the  downside is that the chain attack will  end after an auroboros order unless you  start a chain attack with an oroboros  order if you activate a chain attack  while a level 3 interlink is in use then  you can carry out two auroboros orders  from the interlinked characters now i  found standard chain attacks to be a bit  more effective for my party composition  but if you want to deal a lot of damage  quickly then this is probably the best  way to do it alright i think we've  covered enough ground for today there's  still a lot more to dig into but i think  this is a solid foundation for  first-timers and veterans who might need  a refresher if you'd like to see another  one of these videos let me know in the  comments below in the meantime if you  have any specific xenoblade related  questions feel free to reach out to me  on twitter  jacobdeck thank you so much for watching

